  "description": {
    "architecture": "ResNet38: frozen STFT/log-mel frontend at 32 kHz (1024-sample analysis window, 320-sample hop, 64 mel bins, 50-14000 Hz), an initial convolution block, a basic-block ResNet backbone with layer counts [3,4,6,3], a 512-to-2048 post-ResNet convolution block, global max-plus-mean pooling, a 2048-dimensional fully connected representation, and a 527-class AudioSet head.",
    "preprocessing": "Frozen STFT and log-mel feature extraction at 32000 Hz with a Hann analysis window (the source paper describes a Hamming window; this discrepancy is not resolved). Wrapper preprocessing performs no automatic resampling, downmixing, amplitude normalization, cropping, padding, or truncation; inputs must already satisfy the checkpoint's exact native sample rate and mono-channel contract.",
    "training_objective": "Multilabel audio tagging on AudioSet's 527 sound-event classes, trained with a sigmoid/binary-cross-entropy objective over clip-level labels (officially reported by the paper; not locally reproduced).",
    "checkpoint_behavior": "This checkpoint-specific card represents exactly ResNet38 loaded from the authoritative Zenodo-hosted file ResNet38_mAP=0.434.pth (record 3987831). Strict state-dictionary loading, forward/probability/embedding contracts, determinism, and CPU/MPS device placement were locally verified; published AudioSet mAP was not locally reproduced.",
    "implementation": "Integrated through a shared PANNs wrapper adapter (src/torch_dae/models/panns/model.py::_PannsAudioTagger) over a minimally vendored selection of the official source, preserving upstream forward semantics."
  },
